# vvaharness/util/events.py

The catalogue of logged events: each member name is a stable code and its value is the sentence logged. Data goes in keyword fields, never into the sentence.

Source: `vvaharness/util/events.py` (lines 1-202)
Executor: code
Called from: every module that logs (`log.warning(Event.X, ...)`)

// src: vvaharness/util/events.py:23-202
Event {
  // abstracted: 127 string enumeration members, grouped by area (Stage 1 scope; Stage 2 threat model; Stages 6 to 8; backends transport and TLS; orchestration configuration, environment and checkpoints; preflight, batch and scan; cross-cutting). They carry no logic; they only name log lines.
  // Members whose sentences describe a decision taken elsewhere, kept verbatim:
  S2_HOLLOW_RETRY_ATTEMPTED: "hollow threat model: zero threats on a non-empty repo; re-asking once from the snapshot with no tools"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:46-47
  S2_HOLLOW_RETRY_EMPTY: "the retry also produced nothing s3 can mint a unit from; failing s2 rather than running s3-s8 on zero threats"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:49-50
  S7_DEDUP_UNPARSEABLE: "dedup reply did not parse; keeping every finding (fail-open)"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:64-64
  S8_RESPONSE_UNPARSEABLE: "chain response did not parse; shipping the deterministic report"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:63-63
  TRUNCATED_RETRY: "reply truncated at its output cap; retrying once at a higher cap"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:100-100
  REPLY_CLIPPED_RETRY: "reply clipped at an output budget the route could not grow; retrying once without the effort tier, which shares that budget"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:110-111
  STRUCTURED_REPLY_REJECTED_RETRY: "structured reply rejected; retrying once without the effort tier"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:112-113
  MODEL_REFUSAL_RESEND: "the model refused; re-sending the identical request once"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:114-114
  CKPT_STAGE_DEGRADED: "a cached stage checkpoint recorded unresolved unit failure(s); re-running the step instead of resuming a degraded result"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:140-141
  JSON_INPUT_TRUNCATED: "input exceeds the JSON scan cap; scanning the head only"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:197-197
  RESPONSE_DEGENERATE_ACCEPTED: "degenerate response accepted and used; it raises only after more repeats"   // src: vvaharness/util/events.py:201-202
}
